%I A399151 #9 Aug 20 2026 13:15:20
%S A399151 0,1,2,3,5,7,10,14,19,25,33,43,55,70,88,110,138,170,208,255,309,374,
%T A399151 451,541,646,770,914,1081,1276,1501,1761,2062,2408,2804,3260,3781,
%U A399151 4376,5057,5831,6711,7712,8847,10132,11587,13230,15083,17175,19528,22174,25148,28484
%N A399151 G.f.: (Sum_{k>=1} x^(k^4)/(1 - x^(k^4))) * Product_{k>=1} (1 + x^k).
%C A399151 In general, if m > 1 and g.f. = (Sum_{k>=1} x^(k^m)/(1 - x^(k^m))) * Product_{k>=1} (1 + x^k), then a(n) ~ exp(Pi*sqrt(n/3)) * (3^(1/4)*zeta(m) / (2*Pi*n^(1/4)) + Gamma(1/m)*zeta(1/m) / (m * 2^(2 - 1/m) * 3^(1/4 - 1/(2*m)) * Pi^(1/m) * n^(3/4 - 1/(2*m)))). The formula is valid even for m=1, if we use the limit m->1, then a(n) ~ 3^(1/4)*(2*gamma + log(12*n/Pi^2)) * exp(Pi*sqrt(n/3)) / (4*Pi*n^(1/4)), where gamma is A001620.
%H A399151 Vaclav Kotesovec, <a href="/A399151/b399151.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
%F A399151 a(n) = Sum_{k=1..n} A063775(k)*A000009(n-k).
%F A399151 a(n) ~ exp(Pi*sqrt(n/3)) * (Pi^3/(20*3^(7/4)*n^(1/4)) + Gamma(1/4)*zeta(1/4) / (2^(15/4) * 3^(1/8) * Pi^(1/4) * n^(5/8))).
%t A399151 nmax = 60; CoefficientList[Series[Sum[x^(k^4)/(1-x^(k^4)), {k, 1, Floor[nmax^(1/4)]+1}] * Product[1+x^k, {k, 1, nmax}], {x, 0, nmax}], x]
%Y A399151 Cf. A305082, A399149, A399150.
%Y A399151 Cf. A063775, A000009, A399146.
%K A399151 nonn,new
%O A399151 0,3
